e": "DWS", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " A d&#233;j&#224; vu role play!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn8le16ob10re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}]}, {"type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "engenn8le16ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  &nbsp;Well, Google hasn&rsquo;t heard of this story either, so I think it might be bogus. I haven&rsquo;t checked the internet for strange stories yet, maybe they have some peculiar ones.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  I&rsquo;m sure it will.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  Oh, here&rsquo;s a good one. Have you heard of this one?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Which one?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  This one from England. It is such a strange coincidence.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Read it to me. I&rsquo;m too worn out to get up.", "image": "engenn8le16ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  This story was written in 2001. A girl named Laura Buxton released a helium filled balloon at her grandparents&rsquo; gold wedding anniversary. Her name and address were attached to the balloon along with a note asking the finder to write back.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Wow.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  A reply was received ten days later saying the balloon had been found by another Laura Buxton in the garden of her home 140 miles away.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Yep. That sounds awesome.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  The Lauras were both aged ten and they both had the same pets. They both had a three year old black Labrador and ...<br/>", "image": "engenn8le16ob10re2img01.jpg", "time": "23700", "id": 2}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Sorry Sally. I need to go home. I am wiped out.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  Of course. What are you doing tomorrow?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  I want to see a movie. Have you seen the new Jennifer Aniston flick?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  Yeah, I saw it on Tuesday. It&rsquo;s good. How about a late lunch?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Done. Have fun writing.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  Bye.", "image": "engenn8le16ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "60055", "id": 3}], "coverimg": "engenn8le16ob10re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le16ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Coincidences", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Unbelievable", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the active voice when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject.<br/>You use the passive voice when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\">Children </span>(subject)<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">write</span> stories </span>(object).<br/>Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\">Stories </span>(subject)<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">are written</span></span> (object).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is not always necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span> verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "am/are/is + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The story <span class=\"strong\">was written</span> in 1997.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Past passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "was/were + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Those stories <span class=\"strong\">were told</span> by parents and my grandparents.</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This story was written in 2001.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Her name and address were attached to the balloon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A reply was received ten days later. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The balloon had been found by another Laura Buxton.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience.<br/>When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I have learned English</span> = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.<br/><span class=\"italic\">He has bought a painting</span> = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To emphasize the result of the action, use the simple form.<br/><br/><span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Have you checked the internet for some good stories?</li><li>I've found a lot of good stories that way.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Google hasn't heard of this story either.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I haven't checked the internet for strange stories yet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Have you heard of this one?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " Have you seen the new Jennifer Aniston flick?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bogus", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not real, although pretending to be real", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Google hasn't heard of this story either, so I think it might be bogus.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you find stories on the internet.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "peculiar", "type": "name"}, {"content": "strange, often in an unpleasant way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I haven't checked the internet for strange stories yet, maybe they have some peculiar ones.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to wear out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make someone feel very tired", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Read it to me. I'm too worn out to get up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "helium", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a gas that is lighter than air,  often used for lifting large balloons", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A girl named Laura Buxton released a helium-filled balloon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "wiped out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extremely tired", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sorry Sally.  I need to go home. I am wiped out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "balloon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small coloured bag of thin rubber that you fill with air, used as a child's toy or a decoration", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A girl named Laura Buxton released a helium-filled balloon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Brainstorm various types of coincidence and d&#233;j&#224; vu.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue with a partner about a time you experienced deja vu or a strange coincidence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make your dialogue 8-10 lines long.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Act out your dialogue for your class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about coincidences and strange events. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can write about past events. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can discuss experiences I have and haven't had.", "type": "text"}]}]}